58	/* Max length of numbers for the allocation of temp buffers. Don't forget that
59	 * printf adds an additional \0 at the end!
60	 *
61	 * Sources:
62	 * https://www.exploringbinary.com/maximum-number-of-decimal-digits-in-binary-floating-point-numbers/
63	 *
64	 * UInt16: 3 + 1
65	 * SByte: 3 + 1
66	 * UInt32:
67	 * Int32:
68	 * UInt64:
69	 * Int64:
70	 * Float: 149 + 1
71	 * Double: 767 + 1
72	 */
